' SIS #02 — your FINAL class diagram goes here, as PlantUML (@startuml … @enduml).
' The file is classes.puml (plural), not class.puml as in Week 04.
' Start from the AI's original in models/original/classes.puml, apply your accepted review
' decisions, then render it to models/img/classes.png (or .svg). README section 6.
@startuml
title Domain class diagram — course registration

class Student {
  studentId : ID
  name : String
}

class Course {
  courseCode : String
  title : String
}

class CourseOffering {
  offeringId : ID
  semester : String
  capacity : Integer
  availablePlaces() : Integer «derived»
}

class Enrollment {
  enrollmentId : ID
  enrolledAt : Timestamp
}

Course "1" -- "0..*" CourseOffering : describes
Student "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : holds
CourseOffering "1" -- "0..*" Enrollment : fills places of

note bottom of CourseOffering
  Capacity constraint (R2):
  capacity is a positive whole number (greater than 0);
  enrollment count is between 0 and capacity inclusive;
  availablePlaces() = capacity - enrollment count.
end note

note bottom of Enrollment
  Uniqueness constraint (R3):
  at most one Enrollment per
  (Student, CourseOffering) pair -
  a repeat request is rejected.
  Enrollment is the only association
  between Student and CourseOffering.
end note
@enduml